===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*kʷ-}}{{dercat|ru|ine-bsl-pro}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|когда}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*kogъda}}, from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*koda}}, from which the following words also were derived: {{cog|cu|къгда}}, {{cog|bg|кога}}, {{cog|pl|kiedy}}, {{m|pl|gdy}}, {{cog|sh|када}} / {{m|sh|kada}}, {{cog|sl|kdaj}}, {{cog|cs|kdy}}, {{cog|dsb|gdy}}. Originally the word was probably *koda; compare {{cog|lt|kada||when}}, {{cog|lv|kad}}, Old Indic and {{cog|sa|कदा}}, Avestan ''kadā''. From *koda came *kъdа, possibly under the influence of *kъdе, kъtо. On the other hand, one may perceive in {{m|ru|когда́}} the old instrumental singular *godō of the word {{m|ru|год}} (the old meaning of which was “time, period”) with the interrogative particle ко-, making a genitive singular form *kogo goda (which time?). Thus the -гда ending may have derived from the genitive of {{m|ru|год||period of time}}.

